hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24278","Hashim ibn al-Qasim and Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, both saying: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Rifa'ah al-Adawi, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was delivering a sermon, and I said: A strange man has come asking about his religion; he does not know what his religion is. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to me and left his sermon. Then a chair with worn legs of iron was brought, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat on it. Then he turned to me, teaching me from what Allah had taught him. Then he came to his sermon and completed its end. Abu Abd al-Rahman said in his hadith: Humayd said: He said: I think he saw black wood and thought it was iron."
"24279","Affan narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, who said: Abu Rifa'ah, a man from Banu Adi, said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was delivering a sermon, and he mentioned the hadith."
